% profile: step=one
% A row may hold an unknown, written as a variable in a fact; rows that name
% the same variable share it.  Here a head matches by unification: reading
% p(a) decides U = a, in q(U) as well.  CHR's own head matching never binds a
% constraint's variables, so in CHR this rule would wait until U is known.
% The guard \+ fixed asks that no fixed is present.
p(U). q(U).
fix @ p(a) ==> \+ fixed | fixed.
